  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Suppose $X$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(X)=10.$ What is the value of $det(6X)?$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot X)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(X).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=6$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(6X) & ={6}^{3}\\cdot det(X) \\\\  & =216\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =2160.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
